WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.912
A cell does not simply push proteins through its membrane.

00:00:04.092 --> 00:00:11.080
First, ribosomes attached to rough endoplasmic reticulum make proteins destined for secretion.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:16.688
A transport vesicle buds from the E R and delivers cargo to the Golgi.

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:20.385
The Golgi modifies and sorts that cargo.

00:00:20.565 --> 00:00:25.051
A secretory vesicle then travels toward the cell surface.

00:00:25.231 --> 00:00:28.467
Watch carefully: docking is not release.

00:00:28.647 --> 00:00:35.886
Only when the vesicle membrane fuses with the plasma membrane can its cargo enter the space outside the cell.

00:00:36.066 --> 00:00:39.105
What evidence proves secretion happened?
